       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose of amlodipine (10 mg). Repeating the request doesn't make the dose safe for the patient.\n- **The request still isn't from a prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst, not a clinician. Confirming the order doesn't give you prescribing authority.\n\nA licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient needs to review the order. If they want a dose above the usual range, they can enter it themselves and talk to pharmacy. The hospital's safety checks will probably require that anyway.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms a dose within the standard range, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it then."
